From: Steam-Link-PS5
Subject: hid: clamp report length instead of aborting the title

IHS_HIDReportHolderAddFull asserted holder->reportLength >= len. The host sets
the report length it will parse and may ask for one shorter than the device's
fixed report (seen on a PS5: host requests 48 bytes, a later RequestFullReport
adds the 48-byte report while reportLength was left shorter), so the assert
called abort() and the title crashed a few seconds into every stream. Clamp the
copied length to what the host asked for, and let the first report define the
length when the host has not set one yet. Same guard on the delta path.

diff -ru a/src/hid/report.c b/src/hid/report.c
--- a/src/hid/report.c	2026-10-08 17:01:34.252407430 -0700
+++ b/src/hid/report.c	2026-10-08 20:30:17.998481317 -0700
@@ -83,7 +83,20 @@
 }
 
 void IHS_HIDReportHolderAddFull(IHS_HIDReportHolder *holder, const uint8_t *current, size_t len) {
-    assert(holder->reportLength >= len);
+    /*
+     * The device produces a fixed-size report, but the host decides the report
+     * length it will parse (CHIDMessageToRemote.DeviceStartInputReports.length)
+     * and a RequestFullReport can arrive with that length still shorter than the
+     * device's report. The original assert turned that mismatch into abort(),
+     * killing the whole title a few seconds into a stream once the host asked
+     * for a shorter DualSense report. Clamp instead: never emit more than the
+     * host asked for, and if it has not asked yet, let this report set the size.
+     */
+    if (holder->reportLength == 0) {
+        holder->reportLength = len;
+    } else if (len > holder->reportLength) {
+        len = holder->reportLength;
+    }
     if (DedupAndStash(holder, current, len)) {
         return;
     }
@@ -103,6 +116,11 @@
 
 void IHS_HIDReportHolderAddDelta(IHS_HIDReportHolder *holder, const uint8_t *previous, const uint8_t *current,
                                  size_t len) {
+    if (holder->reportLength == 0) {
+        holder->reportLength = len;
+    } else if (len > holder->reportLength) {
+        len = holder->reportLength;
+    }
     if (DedupAndStash(holder, current, len)) {
         return;
     }
